+# BLUE CURRENT V50.15.0 — PRODUCTION INCIDENT COMMAND
+
+V50.11–V50.15 adds one human-led incident command workflow across production support, observability, and SLO state.
+
+## Incident intake
+
+Production Incident Command reads existing V50.10 support events plus the existing telemetry/observability incident stream.
+
+Open support and observability signals are surfaced together with:
+
+- severity
+- source
+- location when known
+- current owner
+- linked incident reference
+- current status
+
+Blue Current does not automatically open an incident command from those signals.
+
+Incident creation is human initiated.
+
+## Human incident command
+
+Adds:
+
+POST `/api/production-incident-command`
+
+Each incident command can capture:
+
+- title
+- severity
+- incident commander
+- affected restaurants
+- affected domains
+- business impact
+- service impact
+- linked production-support events
+- linked observability incidents
+- current SLO / error-budget state
+- runbook / recovery procedure
+- operator note
+
+Affected restaurant scope is permission checked.
+
+## Incident workflow
+
+Adds:
+
+POST `/api/production-incident-command/:incidentId`
+
+Supported human actions:
+
+- `acknowledge`
+- `contain`
+- `communicate`
+- `recover`
+- `resolve`
+
+### Containment
+
+Containment is recorded as:
+
+`containmentStatus: HUMAN_RECORDED_CONTAINMENT`
+
+Blue Current records that a human incident team performed containment. It does not execute containment.
+
+### Communications
+
+Communication checkpoints record:
+
+- actor
+- detail
+- timestamp
+
+### Recovery evidence
+
+Recovery evidence records:
+
+- actor
+- recovery evidence
+- timestamp
+
+### Resolution
+
+Resolution requires a human-recorded resolution note.
+
+Blue Current does not resolve incidents autonomously.
+
+## SLO and observability linkage
+
+Each incident captures the current existing ReliabilityAutomationService state:
+
+- SLO status
+- breached objectives
+- warning objectives
+- remaining error budget
+
+Existing observability incidents are linked read-only rather than duplicated.
+
+## Safety policy
+
+- `incidentCreationHumanInitiated: true`
+- `containmentHumanDirected: true`
+- `communicationHumanDirected: true`
+- `recoveryEvidenceHumanRecorded: true`
+- `resolutionHumanDeclared: true`
+- `automaticContainment: false`
+- `automaticRemediation: false`
+- `automaticResolution: false`
+- `autonomousProductionChanges: false`
+
+## Current authenticated runtime
+
+The untouched Chefs runtime currently reports:
+
+- status: `incident-command-clear`
+- active incident commands: 0
+- open source signals: 0
+- automatic containment: false
+- automatic remediation: false
+- automatic resolution: false
+- autonomous production changes: false
+
+## Validation
+
+- V50.15 Production Incident Command lifecycle PASS
+- support + observability signal aggregation PASS
+- incident commander / affected scope PASS
+- permission-checked location scope PASS
+- human containment PASS
+- communication checkpoints PASS
+- recovery evidence PASS
+- human resolution PASS
+- V50.10 production-support regression PASS
+- authenticated incident-command GET PASS
+- authoritative database unchanged
+- npm run check PASS
+- 908 JavaScript files
+- 764 client scripts
+- 5,706 unique HTML IDs
+
+## Next
+
+V50.16–V50.20 should build Production Recovery & Post-Incident Review:
+
+- recovery verification
+- restored-service checks
+- affected-location recovery state
+- incident duration / impact summary
+- root-cause and contributing-factor capture
+- corrective actions
+- owner / due-date tracking
+- repeat-risk assessment
+- post-incident executive brief
+- human closure / lessons accepted
+- no autonomous corrective-action execution
